            <ArticleTitle>[Fistula of the right coronary artery near the right ventricle. An echocardiographic study].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>277-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of a 42-year-old woman with a right coronary artery fistula into the right ventricle is reported; she was asymptomatic and a continuous precordial murmur was found on physical examination. We discuss the usefulness and limitation of the Echo 2-D/Doppler findings, concerning this diagnosis, which was only definitively established by angiocardiography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
